course: dictionary
lesson: 9365
title: Sponsor: backing someone with money
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A sponsor is a person or company that gives money to support an event, a team or a person. As a verb, to sponsor means to give that money or support. Look at the words around the word to find out which one it is.
explain: «Sponsored content is an advert made to look like news, and the label "paid for by" tells you someone is selling something.» The clue is "paid for by": someone has paid, so sponsored means a company has paid for the advert.
explain: Sponsor can be a doing word too. «When they want to help, they get sponsored for a challenge» means people promise to give money for the challenge. Try your meaning in the sentence: "they get given money for a challenge" makes sense, so you know you have it right.
fact: A sponsor is a person or company that gives money to support an event, team or person.
fact: To sponsor is to give that money or support. Sponsor can be a noun or a verb.
fact: A sponsored walk works like this: family and friends promise money for each lap or mile, and the money goes to charity.
fact: Sponsors often want their name shown, like on a football team's shirt.
fact: Sponsorship sums use multiplication: money = laps × amount per lap, so 10 laps at £2 each is £20.
exercise: «Videos that are paid adverts are often marked "ad" or "sponsored", sometimes in small print.» What does sponsored mean here? | The video is very funny | Lots of people have watched it | *Someone paid for the video to be made or shown | The video is very old
exercise: Which one is a sponsor? | *A company whose name is on a team's shirt, giving money to the team | A teacher who marks the spelling test | A bus driver who takes children to school | A child who walks with a friend for fun
exercise: Maya's family promise 50p for every lap she runs. What are they, in a sponsored run? | Referees | *Sponsors | Stadium owners | Coaches
test: Ali walks 12 laps and each sponsor pays £3 per lap. How much money does Ali raise from one sponsor? | £15 | £9 | *£36 | £312
test: In a sponsored swim, what does «sponsor me» mean? | Please come and watch me swim | *Please give money for each length I swim | Please stop swimming | Please swim with me
exam: Read «Sponsored content is an advert made to look like news.» Which clue tells you the advert is paid for? | *The label "paid for by" | The word content | Made to look like news | The word advert
